6. SECURITY AND LEAST PRIVILEGE REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

This is mandatory.

Do NOT trust the UI dropdown for authorization.
The selected persona is a requested mode, not the final source of truth.

Implement:
- Authentication layer
- User role verification
- Centralized RBAC/ABAC policy engine
- Least-privilege enforcement
- Deny by default unless explicitly allowed
- Read-only default behavior
- Separate credentials by database + environment + persona
- Time-bound elevated access for risky operations
- Approval gate for writes, destructive actions, or admin-level actions
- Full audit logs for every policy decision and execution attempt

Policy model should support permissions like:
- schema.read
- metadata.read
- query.generate
- query.execute.readonly
- diagnostics.read
- explain.read
- index.review
- health.read
- jobs.read
- ddl.propose
- ddl.execute.approval_required
- admin.elevated.approval_required

