9. AGENT AND TOOLING LOGIC
==================================================

Implement a supervisor pattern.

Supervisor responsibilities:
- Interpret user request
- Determine intent category: schema help, query generation, performance diagnosis, health check, recommendation, change request
- Identify selected database
- Identify selected persona
- Identify target environment
- Request effective permissions from policy engine
- Invoke only allowed sub-agents and connectors
- Ask clarifying questions only if strictly necessary
- Return structured response plus query preview

Sub-agents/services:
- Metadata Agent
- Query Generator Agent
- Validator/Critic Agent
- Safety Agent
- Explanation Agent
- Approval Agent
- Trace/Audit Service

==================================================
10. PERMISSION MODEL
==================================================

Provide a permission matrix for:
- MongoDB x DBA / Operations / Developer
- Oracle x DBA / Operations / Developer
- MySQL x DBA / Operations / Developer
Across:
- Dev
- Staging
- Prod

High-level expected defaults:
- Developer: mostly read-only in dev/staging, heavily restricted in prod
- Operations: health/diagnostics oriented, limited structural change rights
- DBA: broader metadata and tuning access, but risky/destructive actions still require approval
- Production should be stricter than dev/staging
- Destructive or write operations should never run silently

